      "description": "Watch FC Porto vs Alverca highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. On August 9, 2026, the Primeira Liga hosted a tightly contested fixture between FC Porto and Alverca . Both sides took to the pitch with high ambitions, resulting in a match where tactical discipline and clinical execution from the penalty spot would prove to be the deciding factors. VAR Drama Defines the Opening Half The match ignited early when a dangerous challenge by Alverca goalkeeper Matheus Mendes on Andre Silva prompted a VAR review in the 5th minute. After checking the monitor, the referee awarded a penalty. Andre Silva stepped up in the 9th minute and slotted the ball home with his right foot, despite Matheus Mendes getting agonizingly close to making the save. History repeated itself in the closing stages of the first half. In the 41st minute, another VAR intervention for a foul by Nabili Touaizi led to a second penalty for the hosts. Gabriel Veiga took responsibility in the 44th minute, firing accurately past the keeper to double the advantage. The half ended with FC Porto firmly in the driving seat, though Alverca remained competitive in possession. Tactical Shifts and Late Pressure The second half saw a flurry of tactical substitutions as both managers looked to alter the momentum. Alverca pushed for a comeback, with Yaya Bojang forcing a comfortable save from Diogo Costa with a header in the 50th minute. As the clock ticked down, the game grew more physical, leading to bookings for Bojang and Chiquinho . Despite late efforts from Alverca , including a long-range strike from Chiquinho in stoppage time, FC Porto maintained their composure. While the performance might not have been their most dominant, the Dragons managed the final six minutes of added time effectively to secure the win. The match concluded with FC Porto successfully defending their lead against a spirited Alverca side that fought until the final whistle."
